[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:27. A Wet Night]
[00:00.480]Passage 27 | 文章二十七
[00:02.495]A wet night. | 潮湿的夜晚。
[00:05.460]Late in the afternoon, the boys put up their tent in the middle of a field. | 傍晚时分，男孩们把帐篷搭在了田野中央。
[00:12.625]As soon as this was done, they cooked a meal over an open fire. | 刚做完这些，他们就在篝火上做饭。
[00:18.835]They were all hungry and the food smelled good. | 他们都饿了，饭菜闻起来很香。
[00:23.940]After a wonderful meal, they told stories and sang songs by the campfire. | 美餐一顿后，他们围着篝火讲故事、唱歌。
[00:32.330]But sometime later, it began to rain. | 但过了一会儿，天开始下雨了。
[00:37.350]The boys felt tired, so they put out the fire and crept into their tent. | 男孩们感到疲倦，于是熄灭了火，爬进了帐篷。
[00:44.630]Their sleeping bags were warm and comfortable, so they all slept soundly. | 他们的睡袋又暖和又舒服，所以他们都睡得很香。
[00:51.805]In the middle of the night, two boys woke up and began shouting. | 半夜里，两个男孩醒了过来，开始大喊大叫。
[00:58.155]The tent was full of water. | 帐篷里全是水。
[01:01.760]They all leaped out of their sleeping bags and hurried outside. | 他们都从睡袋里跳出来，赶紧跑到外面。
[01:07.605]It was raining heavily, and they found that a stream had formed in the field. | 雨下得很大，他们发现田野里形成了一条小溪。
[01:14.240]The stream wound its way across the field and then flowed right under their tent. | 小溪蜿蜒穿过田野，然后直接流到了他们的帐篷下面。